-**Formulas:** The potential field is constructed as $V(\mathbf{x}) = \sum_{i} \sum_{t} G(\mathbf{x}; \mathbf{p}_{i,t})$, where $G$ is a Gaussian function and $\mathbf{p}_{i,t}$ is the position of particle $i$ at time $t$ [G].
+**Formulas:** The potential field is constructed as $V(\mathbf{x}) = \sum_{i} \sum_{t} \exp\left(-\frac{\|\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{p}_{i,t}\|^2}{2\sigma^2}\right)$, where $\mathbf{p}_{i,t}$ is the position of particle $i$ at time $t$, and $\sigma$ controls the blobby spread [S1, unofficial].
 
